  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual metaphor of Black people as an object of exclusion",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material (the woman holding the rusty funnel) and the textual material ('black people' and 'anthing that doesn't belong to them'), which together form a racist analogical mapping. The user is implicitly identifying with the act of presenting or assigning value to the object (the funnel), thereby projecting themselves onto the dehumanizing metaphor. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the framing of the image and the hateful intent create an implicit projection where the viewer is positioned as the one assigning the metaphorical meaning to the visual and textual elements.",
